{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals","id":869805,"title":"Question on feeding on animals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-20T18:57:04-07:00","id":869805,"title":"Question on feeding on animals","content":"When a kindred feed on am animal and gain the vitae / size of the animal does this kill the animal? I do belive that is what that section is saying but I am unsure if it would kill the animal because it is not directly stated.<br /> <br /> The alternative way I could read it is that beyond the 1 vitae per size, the beast cannot supply further vitae for a set time. Since the general rule of 1 lethal per vitae drained it is possible for the animal to survive if it is not killed by default.<br /> <br /> The main reason I ask is because if this is the proper reading of it you could truly have a vampire that refuses to feed from humans and refuses to kill animals. Or even just buying a cow for an easy source of vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T20:23:13-07:00","id":869862,"title":"","content":"You really could have a vampire who feeds solely on animals ( and not kill them ). I think with the healing process it would take a couple of cows, but feeding one per size wouldn't kill them. Just leave them drained and miserable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T20:33:49-07:00","id":869870,"title":"","content":"Had to ask because I had assumed it'd kill the animal. Only reading it over did I realize there was no such direct statement. Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T09:29:07-07:00","id":870275,"title":"","content":"I think the intent is that draining all of an animal's blood (which would kill them) yields Vitae equal to the animal's size. It's not explicitly stated this way, but it seems odd to me that you'd be able to drain a point worth of Vitae from a size 1 animal and leave it in relatively fine health. There's not much blood in a rat, but yet you can get a whole Vitae our of one without killing it? That would imply that rats have a <i>greater</i> concentration of Vitae to blood than humans, which doesn't seem right. I would say if you want to drain an animal of less than its full Size in Vitae, it should take a proportional amount of lethal damage to its health. (i.e. taking 1 Vitae from a size 4 animal should deal 1/4 of its health in lethal to it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T09:41:25-07:00","id":870285,"title":"","content":"Proportional damage does sound more in line with the intent of that section. It'd be an easy enough house rule for dealing with what happens when an animal isn't completely drained. Thank you.<br /> <br /> So in this case my example before of a vampire owning a cow would not work but a vampire owning a whole farm. Which does feel more thematic for a vampire to operate an entire farm for a vitae supply instead of a single cow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T09:45:07-07:00","id":870289,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it is like the MAX amount. like Max for a human ( size+stamina dots.) so you could on average say take a total of 7 which would leave them dying. Concept the same for a rat which has 1. you take that 1 you would leave it dying? <br /> <br /> I dont see a problem of a vampire feeding off a whole farm. Your animals would be sort of miserable, but it could be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:02:38-07:00","id":870304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=870285#post870285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Proportional damage does sound more in line with the intent of that section. It'd be an easy enough house rule for dealing with what happens when an animal isn't completely drained. Thank you.<br /> <br /> So in this case my example before of a vampire owning a cow would not work but a vampire owning a whole farm. Which does feel more thematic for a vampire to operate an entire farm for a vitae supply instead of a single cow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the idea of a vampire cattle rancher wuth a whole farm of sickly, anemic cows, rotating which ones are being fed from and which ones are in recovery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:54:46-07:00","id":870495,"title":"","content":"I agree, if you drain not-too-small animals of all of their vitae you are not necessarily draining them of all of their blood, but you are most certainly draining them of all of their<i> life</i>. Taking little sips and applying Charlaquin's rotating trick is indeed the best way to keep them alive.<br /> <br /> Indeed I had a couple of NPC providing exactly that kind of service to Neonates in exchange for favors. They also ghouled the local kosher butcher, he ritually killed goats over the spot where their Mekhet mate (Auspex 5, Protean 1) chilled out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","user":"Ophion","date":", whoops 04-21-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:22:00-07:00","id":878295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=870495#post870495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, if you drain not-too-small animals of all of their vitae you are not necessarily draining them of all of their blood, but you are most certainly draining them of all of their<i> life</i>. Taking little sips and applying Charlaquin's rotating trick is indeed the best way to keep them alive.<br /> <br /> Indeed I had a couple of NPC providing exactly that kind of service to Neonates in exchange for favors. They also ghouled the local kosher butcher, he ritually killed goats over the spot where their Mekhet mate (Auspex 5, Protean 1) chilled out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I must disagree.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/305707-what-s-the-blood-economy-like-in-your-games?p=307643#post307643\">I've dealt with this before.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:29:44-07:00","id":878302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=870275#post870275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the intent is that draining all of an animal's blood (which would kill them) yields Vitae equal to the animal's size. It's not explicitly stated this way, but it seems odd to me that you'd be able to drain a point worth of Vitae from a size 1 animal and leave it in relatively fine health. There's not much blood in a rat, but yet you can get a whole Vitae our of one without killing it? That would imply that rats have a <i>greater</i> concentration of Vitae to blood than humans, which doesn't seem right. I would say if you want to drain an animal of less than its full Size in Vitae, it should take a proportional amount of lethal damage to its health. (i.e. taking 1 Vitae from a size 4 animal should deal 1/4 of its health in lethal to it).</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, per p95 Blood &amp; Smoke, Size 4-5 animal provides 3 blood points or Vitae. +1 Vitae for each size increase.<br /> So man-sized is 4 Blood Points, Large 5, Heavy(Cattle) 6.<br /> <br /> I don't remember what the small animals give you. Can't find my book.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:01:22-07:00","id":878369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878302#post878302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, per p95 Blood &amp; Smoke, Size 4-5 animal provides 3 blood points or Vitae. +1 Vitae for each size increase.<br /> So man-sized is 4 Blood Points, Large 5, Heavy(Cattle) 6.<br /> <br /> I don't remember what the small animals give you. Can't find my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's right there in the paragraph you quoted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Animal blood</b> is a challenging meal that provides only limited sustenance for the youngest of Kindred. Size 0 animals provide no nourishment. Size 1 animals provide one point of Vitae. For example, a large rat will provide a single point of Vitae. Size 2-3 animals provide two Vitae each. Size 4-5 animals provide 3. Each point of Size above that adds one more Vitae available. </div> </div> </div>Anyway, my point was that I'm pretty sure the intent is for you get that much Vitae for drinking the animal to death. If you wanted a house rule for only partially drinking an animal, it should probably take a proportional amount of damage. So if it has 1 Vitae, you've got to drink it dry to get anything. If it has 2 vitae, it should take half its health in lethal damage for each Vitae you take. If it has 3 Vitae, it should take 1/3 of its health for each Vitae you take. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:07:58-07:00","id":878376,"title":"","content":"I bet there's a vampire out there with a smug smirk and two elephants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:11:48-07:00","id":878380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878295#post878295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I must disagree.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/305707-what-s-the-blood-economy-like-in-your-games?p=307643#post307643&quot;\">I've dealt with this before.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I read your post, and I fail to see how it's a counter-argument. Yes, We are talking about very large quantities of fluid, and it would take a long time to get through it all. In what way does that mean it can't be done?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:41:05-07:00","id":878401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878376#post878376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet there's a vampire out there with a smug smirk and two elephants.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there's one with an even more smug smirk and two <i>ghouled </i>elephants. Both of which have mastered the physical Disciplines. Including Celerity. Yes, a ghoul elephant with Celerity 5. That's how I roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:58:26-07:00","id":878582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878380#post878380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I read your post, and I fail to see how it's a counter-argument. Yes, We are talking about very large quantities of fluid, and it would take a long time to get through it all. In what way does that mean it can't be done?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've had this discussion in another thread, though with humans. Your earlier statement kind of contradicts this attitude, too. I don't think you have to drink it all to get all the vitae. Volume of blood in a living thing doesn't really matter in my mind.<br /> <br /> With humans, I don't think drinking all Vitae drains all their blood. It doesn't really make any sense, given you can survive having all your vitae being taken.<br /> <br /> With animals, therefore, there are two interpretations that seem to make sense:<br /> <br /> 1. It's the same as humans. Which means drinking all their vitae doesn't drink all their blood and they can potentially survive it (though size 1 critters won't give you much time to stabilize them).<br /> <br /> 2. It's not the same, and you do have to drink all their blood to get all their vitae. But this means they'll be dead before you finish drinking, and they probably shouldn't survive half-feedings. It makes less sense to me, but it's valid as anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T07:39:14-07:00","id":878713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878582#post878582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've had this discussion in another thread, though with humans. Your earlier statement kind of contradicts this attitude, too. I don't think you have to drink it all to get all the vitae. Volume of blood in a living thing doesn't really matter in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't actually say drink all of their blood. I said drink them to death. Vitae is life, not blood, and the way I see it, if you drink enough of their blood to kill them, you've taken all of their Vitae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878582#post878582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With humans, I don't think drinking all Vitae drains all their blood. It doesn't really make any sense, given you can survive having all your vitae being taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but if you drink all of a human's vitae, their health track will be full of lethal damage, which is exactly what would happen to an animal under my proposed proportional damage house rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878582#post878582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With animals, therefore, there are two interpretations that seem to make sense:<br /> <br /> 1. It's the same as humans. Which means drinking all their vitae doesn't drink all their blood and they can potentially survive it (though size 1 critters won't give you much time to stabilize them).<br /> <br /> 2. It's not the same, and you do have to drink all their blood to get all their vitae. But this means they'll be dead before you finish drinking, and they probably shouldn't survive half-feedings. It makes less sense to me, but it's valid as anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I've said a few times now, I'm pretty sure the intent of the rule is that if you use up the animal, you get its full amount of Vitae. Really, there is no official rule for the animal surviving or for getting less than its full Vitae capacity from it. What I'm saying is that if you want such a thing to be possible, you could make it work like it works on humans by dealing an amount of lethal damage to the animal proportional to the amount of Vitae you drink. Chattanos seemed to try to counter this by linking to a post where he talks a lot about how much blood a pig has and how it would take a long time to drink gallons of blood. I responded that his post was accurate, but really has nothing to do with my proposed house rule, which is concerned with amount of Vitae and amount of Health, not amount of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T07:59:31-07:00","id":878727,"title":"","content":"I would propose an addition to that houserule. If you drain more than half or two vitae from an animal (whichever is lower) they gain the drained condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:04:38-07:00","id":878734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878727#post878727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would propose an addition to that houserule. If you drain more than half or two vitae from an animal (whichever is lower) they gain the drained condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T12:40:09-07:00","id":884821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878582#post878582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've had this discussion in another thread, though with humans. Your earlier statement kind of contradicts this attitude, too. I don't think you have to drink it all to get all the vitae. Volume of blood in a living thing doesn't really matter in my mind.<br /> <br /> With humans, I don't think drinking all Vitae drains all their blood. It doesn't really make any sense, given you can survive having all your vitae being taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you get that? Your limited by their stamina and wound levels.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878582#post878582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With animals, therefore, there are two interpretations that seem to make sense:<br /> <br /> 1. It's the same as humans. Which means drinking all their vitae doesn't drink all their blood and they can potentially survive it (though size 1 critters won't give you much time to stabilize them).<br /> <br /> 2. It's not the same, and you do have to drink all their blood to get all their vitae. But this means they'll be dead before you finish drinking, and they probably shouldn't survive half-feedings. It makes less sense to me, but it's valid as anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sorry the books are clear. The blood is the carrier of the vitae unless your are a breathe drinker.<br /> Take a look at the rules for blood bags if disagree.<br /> Now you are free to house rule any way you like but it is clear that the new rules were to discourage blood banking from non-human sources.<br /> <br /> One caveat is to fix the size system or base it on body volume<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T12:41:32-07:00","id":884823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=878376#post878376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet there's a vampire out there with a smug smirk and two elephants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per RAW each elephant could only supply 7 points of Vitae.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:00:56-07:00","id":884888,"title":"","content":"Per raw size five gives 3 vitae then +1 per size greater. Elephants are Size 14 so they can provide 12 vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T05:48:57-07:00","id":885315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=884821#post884821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you get that? Your limited by their stamina and wound levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you drink all the Vitae you can from a human being, they are at full lethal damage. They can survive this with a single First Aid roll. Therefore, drinking all of a human being's vitae does not drain even half their blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=884821#post884821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sorry the books are clear. The blood is the carrier of the vitae unless your are a breathe drinker.<br /> Take a look at the rules for blood bags if disagree.<br /> Now you are free to house rule any way you like but it is clear that the new rules were to discourage blood banking from non-human sources.<br /> <br /> One caveat is to fix the size system or base it on body volume</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you're talking about here. I'm not house ruling anything, and I'm not sure how any of this is relevant to what I said and what you quoted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T21:14:05-07:00","id":886942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=885315#post885315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you drink all the Vitae you can from a human being, they are at full lethal damage. They can survive this with a single First Aid roll. Therefore, drinking all of a human being's vitae does not drain even half their blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good point! I don't know how I failed to consider that full lethal doesn't automatically mean death. Death only occurs at full aggravated and as you said first aid could prevent bleeding out. That simplifies things a lot. The vampire would just have to patch them up after a full feeding and let them heal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T02:48:27-07:00","id":887055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=886942#post886942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a good point! I don't know how I failed to consider that full lethal doesn't automatically mean death. Death only occurs at full aggravated and as you said first aid could prevent bleeding out. That simplifies things a lot. The vampire would just have to patch them up after a full feeding and let them heal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Patch them up... I'm sorry, but what does &quot;Patch them up&quot; means in regards to a person missing blood? It's not like you have a wound to patch up. In my opinion, the man needs a blood transfusion, (or a point of vitae from you, reinforced with your will to make them a ghoul). But other than that - there's no first aid for a victim drained fully, you need certain procedures to do, if you want to save them mundanely. <br /> <br /> Just because a rule says you can &quot;make a roll to help heal lethal/stabilise them&quot; doesn't mean it's feasable or possible without tools in some certain situations. (like having your damage be done from missing blood/vitae, with no proper wound to actually take care of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T06:25:06-07:00","id":887117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=884888#post884888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per raw size five gives 3 vitae then +1 per size greater. Elephants are Size 14 so they can provide 12 vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> According to this link,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?413156-nWOD-Seeking-expanded-Size-table&amp;p=9328229#post9328229\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...29#post9328229</a><br /> Size 5-6 = Man-sized (Cougar, Ape, Condor, Deer)<br /> <i>Really? A cougar is usually bigger than a man or a deer.</i><br /> <br /> Size 6-8 = Large (Horse, Bear, Dolphin, Komodo Dragon)<br /> Size 9-13 = Heavy (Cattle, Moose, Bull Seal)<br /> Size 11-15 = Huge Animal (Elephant, Hippo, Sea Lion, Orca)<br /> <br /> RAW, per p95 Blood &amp; Smoke, Size 4-5 animal provides 3 blood points or Vitae. +1 Vitae for each size increase.<br /> So man-sized is 4 Blood Points, Large 5, Heavy(Cattle) 6.<br /> <br /> I read that as +1 per step on the size class chart. <br /> Haven't the new size chart. And I can't lay my hands on Blood and Smoke at the moment.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T06:57:12-07:00","id":887130,"title":"","content":"My book has different rules. It's Blood &amp; Smoke, too, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood &amp; Smoke, p95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal blood is a challenging meal that provides only limited sustenance for the youngest of Kindred. Size 0 animals provide no nourishment. Size 1 animals provide one point of Vitae. For example, a large rat will provide a single point of Vitae. Size 2-3 animals provide two Vitae each. Size 4-5 animals provide 3. Each point of Size above that adds one more Vitae available.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:18:56-07:00","id":887142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=887130#post887130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My book has different rules. It's Blood &amp; Smoke, too, though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to dig mine then. And I have no idea where it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:43:58-07:00","id":887251,"title":"","content":"Can confirm, I have both Blood &amp; Smoke and VtR second edition (same book, different title but still...) and Nofather's quote is also what both of my copies say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:46:07-07:00","id":887293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=887251#post887251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can confirm, I have both Blood &amp; Smoke and VtR second edition (same book, different title but still...) and Nofather's quote is also what both of my copies say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to rework that article. However that is still a lot of blood.<br /> Size 6=4<br /> Size=7= 5<br /> Size8=6<br /> <br /> Basically size 6 and above, animal vitae equals is size-2.<br /> Assuming All cattle are size 7 and 5% is blood by weight, we are still looking at 7 gallons for 5 vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T11:09:32-07:00","id":887313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=887293#post887293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to rework that article. However that is still a lot of blood.<br /> Size 6=4<br /> Size=7= 5<br /> Size8=6<br /> <br /> Basically size 6 and above, animal vitae equals is size-2.<br /> Assuming All cattle are size 7 and 5% is blood by weight, we are still looking at 7 gallons for 5 vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, you're probably not completely exsanguinating the animal to get that much vitae. If we compare to feeding from humans,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred can pull a number of Vitae from a mortal equal to the mortal\u2019s unmodified Health dots. Every point of Vitae she takes causes one point of lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means if you drink all of the Vitae from a human, their health track will be full of lethal damage. That still leaves a number of turns of bleeding out equal to their health dots before the track is full of aggravated damage and they actually die, and you kind of need to have blood to bleed out. Yet, a vampire that continued to drink that blood would not gain Vitae from it, ergo we are forced to conclude that you don't have to drink all of a vessel's blood to get all of its Vitae.<br /> <br /> So again, we're back to &quot;if you take the full amount of Vitae from an animal, fill its health track with lethal damage. If you want a house rule to allow you to take less than the full amount of vitae, deal a proportional amount of lethal damage to it.&quot; And the amount of actual blood that needs to be consumed for this to happen is an abstraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T11:44:57-07:00","id":887344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=887313#post887313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again though, you're probably not completely exsanguinating the animal to get that much vitae. If we compare to feeding from humans,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That means if you drink all of the Vitae from a human, their health track will be full of lethal damage. That still leaves a number of turns of bleeding out equal to their health dots before the track is full of aggravated damage and they actually die, and you kind of need to have blood to bleed out. Yet, a vampire that continued to drink that blood would not gain Vitae from it, ergo we are forced to conclude that you don't have to drink all of a vessel's blood to get all of its Vitae.<br /> <br /> So again, we're back to &quot;if you take the full amount of Vitae from an animal, fill its health track with lethal damage. If you want a house rule to allow you to take less than the full amount of vitae, deal a proportional amount of lethal damage to it.&quot; And the amount of actual blood that needs to be consumed for this to happen is an abstraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>7 Vitae one for each health level. Humans have about seven pints. How damage do they take if left untreated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:14:36-07:00","id":887377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=887344#post887344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 Vitae one for each health level. Humans have about seven pints. How damage do they take if left untreated?</div> </div> </div> </div>If he has seven health boxes? Seven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cronicles of Darkness pg 95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a character\u2019s rightmost Health box has lethal damage marked in it, he takes another point of damage each minute (upgrading existing lethal damage to aggravated) until he receives medical attention, mundane or supernatural.<br /> If a character\u2019s Health track is filled with aggravated damage, he\u2019s dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, later on the same page:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if a character has all her Health boxes full of lethal damage \u2014 she\u2019s bleeding out. She can\u2019t recover from that without urgent medical attention and emergency surgery. </div> </div> </div>So, for like the 5th time in this thread, a character who has had all of their Vitae extracted from them by a vampire is unconscious and will continue to bleed out for a number of minutes equal to their health boxes until they die. Ergo they must still have blood to bleed out, ergo you do not have to completely exsanguinate someone to completely drain them of Vitae.<br /> <br /> If you want to get really anal about it, it's half. One health track full of lethal gets you all of their Vitae, and they can still take that same amount of damage a second time before they've bled out. But the truth is, blood just doesn't correspond to health boxes 1:1 like that. It's an abstraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T22:38:59-07:00","id":887905,"title":"","content":"My Tismanu had a farm and the Coil so he never needed to go off of animal blood. His Sire made sure he never tasted human blood, so he didn't have to deal with the withdrawals either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T11:37:17-07:00","id":888408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=887117#post887117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> According to this link,<br /> <br /> <i>Really? A cougar is usually bigger than a man or a deer.</i><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's my understanding that cougar males average less that 150 lbs, so I would disagree with that assertion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:07:11-07:00","id":888543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/869805-question-on-feeding-on-animals?p=888408#post888408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's my understanding that cougar males average less that 150 lbs, so I would disagree with that assertion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I've been face to face with a cougar, they really aren't that big. Now, bears, caribou, moose, those get big. I live in Pacific Northwest of the US, these things are concerns when you go hiking/camping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:27:04-07:00","id":889255,"title":"","content":"Well any animal of roughly human weight or or more can maim or kill a man, and predatory teeth and claws are force multipliers. Heck, a doe can tear you up bad or knock you out with just her front hooves.<br /> Think of how much damage a pissed off house cat can do, now imagine one almost a big as yourself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 05-12-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:17:35-07:00","id":889352,"title":"","content":"+1ing the whole small(ish) wild animals are dangerous (if not deadly) to humans. Considering how much the average chimpanzee weighs (~30-40#) and how much damage they can do to human beings (amputate limbs, maul major features, break bones, other massive mechanical injuries), a house cat a quarter of your weight will be able to do some serious damage to you. I'd be wary of any wild animal (or animal I don't know) that weighs more than 30# or so. Even a badger can cause some significant injuries and the very, very rare wolverine is well-known to kill things that are substantially larger than them (imagine something that death-rolls just your trachea).<br /> <br /> Ironically, if you talk to zoologists they tell you that even these &quot;small&quot; creatures are, in fact, (&quot;charismatic&quot;) megafauna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}